\label{sec:b-precision-anchors}
T1 uses E1 pools and twelve paired configurations per OpenAI dataset. Two five-round JHQ repetitions bracket baseline runs; medians combine geometrically. Equal-configuration FP32/TF32 means are 0.956/0.964. Both reuse TF32-trained caches, changing add/query arithmetic.
\begin{table}[tbp]
\centering
\caption[Same-session precision anchors]{T1 at recall 0.97, batch 1,000. Baseline ratios are interpolation / strict measured threshold; FP32/TF32 is interpolated. All methods share a session, unlike D's archived baselines.}
\label{tab:b-precision-anchors}
\footnotesize\setlength{\tabcolsep}{3pt}
\input{tables/full-review/precision-anchors}
\end{table}
The OpenAI-3072 RaBitQ bracket (0.9669--0.9796 recall) shows grid sensitivity. These anchors neither replace E1 nor provide FP32 retraining.

